      "message": "Above comment was discussed in \nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/base/+/1179828/9..11/services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java#b6529\n\nAfter offline sync with lucas, if losing the TRUSTED is the problem, \nhere is the summary of what we suggested:\nA28 -\u003e use isReassignmentChanged(nri) with getNewSatisfier() to handle TRUSTED case.\nSee \nhttps://android-https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/base/+/1179828/10/services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java#6348\nWhere the newDefaultNetwork will be null in losing TRUSTED case instead of equal the old one.\nProperly handle default clean up in makeDefault(),\nIIUC there is no API in netd to handle this, too.\n\nA33 -\u003e do not return fast if network is null.",
